From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:31:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 65/67] Standings: change by the (10 - standing) formula, with
 derived standings

Mission standing changes were added as they are, so +0.005 for a level 1
mission instead of 0.5% of the way to 10, and they were also multiplied by
1.1 - security, so an agent in a 1.0 system gave a sixth of what one in a 0.5
system gave.  The client already applied the change properly to what it was
told, so it showed standings the server didn't have until the next login.

- a mission moves a standing that fraction of the way to +10 (or -10 for a
  loss), the way the client does it, so it can't pass +-10
- no security scaling
- the faction change also moves the faction's friends up and its enemies
  down, by change x their standing towards it / 10 and no further than that
  standing.  A loss only lowers its friends.  New setting DerivedStandings
  (true) in the standings block; the client is told about each one
- Agent2CharMissionMultiplier is used now (1.0)
- the raw add used for killing pirates stays as it was, but stops at +-10
